  - aggregation
  - sensitivity analysis
  - identifiability
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.3 preserves the
  post-v0.3.2 model-semantics-v21 baseline after completion of the second
  independent/adversarial scientific audit. That audit covered Areas A-N, repaired
  and reverified all 15 recorded AV2 findings, and closed with no open P0-P3
  scientific finding. This release records a reviewed scientific-hardening baseline;
  it does not establish empirical archaeological validity or prove model correctness.
